\section{Construction of a lifting of the prime divisor}


\vskip.5truecm 
\noindent
As we mentioned just after the Corollary \ref{equal-p-0},
the corollary holds for the dimension of the variety $N=1$.
So, from now on, we assume  $N\geq 2$.

 \begin{prop-def}\label{zs}{\rm (Zariski, see eg.{\cite[VI, 1.3]{ko}})}
    Let $E$ be a prime divisor over a  variety $A'$ defined over a field $k$ and appear  on $\psi:A''\to A' $.
    Let $Q\in A''$ be the generic point of $E$ and $Q_0\in A'$ the  image of $Q$.
    Then, 
 we have a sequence of varieties $A'_0,A'_1, \ldots, A'_n$  and birational maps as follows:
 \begin{enumerate}
 \item[$(0)$]
 $A'_0=A'$, $\psi'_0=\psi$.
 \item[$(i)$] If  $\psi'_i: A''\dashrightarrow
  A'_i$ is already defined, then let  $Q_i=\psi_i(Q)$.
 Let $A'_{i+1}=Bl_{Q_i}A'_i$ and  $\psi'_{i+1}: A''\dashrightarrow
  A'_{i}$ be the induced map.
 \item[$(n)$] Then, the final birational map $\psi'_{n}:A''\dashrightarrow
  A'_n$ is isomorphic at $Q$, 
 {\it i.e.,} $E$ appears on $A'_n$.
 \end{enumerate}
 Here, $Bl_{Q_i}A'_i$ is the blow-up of $A'_i$ at $Q_i$.
 Let $\varphi'_i:A'_i\to A'_{i-1}$ be the blow-up morphism and $E_i\subset A'_i$ be the exceptional divisor dominating $Q_i$.
 We call this sequence $A'_n\to\cdots\to A'_1\to A'_0=A'$ the {\sl Zariski sequence for $E$ over $A'$}.
 \end{prop-def}

 Note that 
 if $Q_0\in A'$ is a non-singular point, then $Q_i$'s are all  non-singular for $i=1,\ldots, n-1$.
 Indeed, this is proved inductively.
 As $A'_1 $ is the blow-up at a non-singular point $Q_0$, it follows that $A'_1$ and $E_1$ are non-singular in a neighborhood of ${\psi'_1}^{-1}(Q_0)$.
 Since $Q_1\in {\psi'_1}^{-1}(Q_0)$, it follows that $Q_1$ is again a non-singular point.
 In the same way, we obtain that $Q_i$'s are all non-singular.



