[H_{n-1,1},g(r,m+1-r)]&=g(r+1,m+1-r)-2g(r,m+2-r).
\end{align*}
Thus, we find that \eqref{Eq903-4} holds for the case $r+s=m+1$.
We can prove \eqref{Eq903-5}, \eqref{Eq903-8} and \eqref{Eq903-8.5} similarly.
