\noindent
(iii) Inspired by quantum gravity approaches like loop quantum gravity \cite{ashte} and string theory, dark space-time might exist as a superposition of multiple geometric states. Quantum coherence between dark and ordinary space-time could lead to nonlocal effects.

\noindent
(v) If dark space-time interacts weakly with ordinary space-time via gravity, it could be modeled as an entangled sector of the universe. 

