%\hspace*{6cm} $c$ switches to mode $\negFast$; \\
%\hspace*{5cm} {\bf else}\\
%\hspace*{6cm} $c$ switches to mode $\plusFast$; \\

\noindent
{\bf Remark.}
Each meeting in the algorithm has to involve at least one moving agent.
More precisely, if {\tt Event B} happens at some node $u$ in some round, then there is at least one fast agent or one slow agent at node $u$ in this round.
Hence, {\tt Event B} cannot happen, if there are only $(x-2)$ sentinel agents at their base.
In the pseudo-code for {\tt Event B},  the following types of meetings are considered:
