\begin{abstract} \iffalse We introduce a neural-network scheme for the numerical solution of backward stochastic Volterra integral equations (BSVIEs).
The algorithm is demonstrated on test cases with up to 20 spatial dimensions, including fully coupled FSDE–BSVIE systems in which the forward SDE’s drift and diffusion depend on the BSVIE solution processes themselves.

On the theory side we provide a non-asymptotic error bound for the decoupled setting where the forward component is a stochastic Volterra integral equation; the bound consists of an a posteriori term plus an $O(\Delta t^{1/2})$ contribution from time discretization.

