but we overload the syntactic form of the associated expression here, as is common.
The sorts of the subterms are determined by their names.
We denote evaluation contexts with names starting with $E$,
expression subterms with $e$, and value subterms with $v$.
From this description, we generate a well-formedness rule for each context
