\subsection{Distance to the marginals}

In the same framework as previously defined, another divergence function found in the literature is based on the Euclidean norm distance to \(q\). Taking the entropy function defined by \(\phi(x)\defeq \frac{1}{2}\vert x- 1\vert ^2 \) on \(\R^{N\!+\!M}\) leads for any \(\psi \in \R^{N\!+\!M}\) to the following divergence: 
\[
\mathrm{F}(\psi) = \frac{1}{2}\| \psi - q \|_2^2.
\]
The Legendre transform of \(\phi\) is defined for any \(y \in \R\) as:
\[
\phi^*\!(y) = \frac{1}{2} y^2 + y,
\]
which is \(\mathcal{C}^2\) and strongly-convex on \(\R\).

