\section{Market Dynamics}
The mid-price $S(t)$ and variance $V(t)$ follow the Heston model with permanent market impact:
\begin{align}
dS(t) &= \left( \mu - \eta \nu(t) \right) S(t) dt + \sqrt{V(t)} S(t) dW_S(t), \label{eq:price_heston} \\
dV(t) &= \kappa \left( \theta - V(t) \right) dt + \xi \sqrt{V(t)} dW_v(t), \label{eq:variance_heston}
\end{align}
where parameters are defined in Table~\ref{tab:parameters}. The execution price includes non-linear temporary impact:
\begin{equation}
\tilde{S}(t) = S(t) - \epsilon \nu(t)^\beta, \label{eq:execution_price}
\end{equation}
with $\epsilon > 0$ and $\beta \in (0,1]$ (e.g., $\beta = 0.5$ for square-root impact).

