with $F_{\pm}(\kk)=\epsilon(\kk) \pm \mathcal{M}(\kk)$, $\mathcal{M}(\kk)=M+B k^2$, $\epsilon(\kk)=D k^2$ and the projection operator $P_0$ is given in Eq.(\ref{Eq:projection0}). The first term in $H_{\pm}(\kk)$ is diagonal. The Hamiltonian matrix $H_{+-}(\kk)$ is given by  
\begin{eqnarray}
