with $k_\pm=k_x\pm i k_y $ and $(\gs_j)_{\pm} = g_{j,x} \pm i g_{j,y}$ for different $j$ values. Below, we will set the moir\'e reciprocal lattice vector $\gs_1 = \bs{0}$. 

From the above numerical calculations of the wave function from Eq.(\ref{Eq:wave function delta BHZ2}), we know that the c-electrons should mainly come from the first diagonal matrix element $F_+(\kk+\gs_1)=F_+(\kk)$ in the block $H_+(\kk)$, while the f-electron is mainly from the block $H_-(\kk)$. Since c-electrons should weakly depend on moir\'e potential for $\Delta_0>0$, we make the approximation of neglecting %all the off-diagonal components of 
