\subsection{Experiments Setup}
\subsubsection{\textbf{Baselines}}
We select ID-based traditional and ID-based multimodal collaborative filtering methods as baselines:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{BPR}~\cite{rendle2012bpr} is a traditional method based on Bayesian personalized ranking.
  \item \textbf{LightGCN}~\cite{he2020lightgcn} is a traditional method of lightweight graph convolutional neural networks.
  \item \textbf{SL}~\cite{wu2024effectiveness} is LightGCN using the Softmax loss.
  \item \textbf{VBPR}~\cite{he2016vbpr} is a multimodal method that introduces visual information based on BPR.
  \item \textbf{DualGNN}~\cite{wang2021dualgnn} is a multimodal method that constructs a user-user graph using multimodal information.
  \item \textbf{LATTICE}~\cite{zhang2021mining} is a multimodal method that constructs an item-item graph using multimodal information.
  \item \textbf{SLMRec}~\cite{tao2022self} is a multimodal method that introduces contrastive learning.
  \item \textbf{FREEDOM}~\cite{zhou2023tale} is a multimodal method that optimizes graph construction and graph denoising.
  \item \textbf{SOIL}~\cite{su2024soil} is a multimodal method that proposes a second-order interest graph.
  \item \textbf{BeFA}~\cite{fan2024befa} is a multimodal method that corrects multimodal features based on user behavior.
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection{\textbf{Metrics}}
Similar to existing work~\cite{zhou2023tale, su2024soil, fan2024befa}, we use common evaluation metrics in the top-K recommendation task: Recall (R@K) and Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain (N@K), where K is set to $\{5, 10, 20, 50\}$.

\subsubsection{\textbf{Implementation Details}}
All methods are implemented based on the MMRec framework~\cite{zhou2023mmrec}. The dataset is divided into training, validation, and test sets in an 8:1:1 ratio. We implement all methods using PyTorch 2.4.0 and train them on a single Nvidia RTX 4090. All methods use the Adam optimizer, with a batch size of 1024, 1000 training epochs, and 20 early stopping epochs. The hidden dimension is set to 64. The parameters of all baselines are set to the optimal results of the corresponding datasets. The fusion weight $\alpha$ of IDFREE is set to 0.5, and other hyperparameters are adjusted using grid search. The $k$ in \S~\ref{subsubsec:m_graph_construction} ranges from $ \{5, 10, 20\} $. The $\rho$ and $L$  in \S~\ref{subsubsec:augmented_user_item_graph_encoder} ranges from $ \{0.7, 0.8, 0.9\} $ and $ \{2, 3, 4, 5, 10, 15, 20\} $, respectively. The $\tau$ in \S~\ref{subsec:loss} ranges from $ \{0.1, 0.2, 0.3 \} $. 

